{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/900875-what-you-should-get-for-not-joining-a-covenant","id":900875,"title":"What you should get for NOT joining a Covenant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-27T06:20:46-07:00","id":900875,"title":"What you should get for NOT joining a Covenant","content":"It seems not right that not joining a covenant would not give any game mechanic advantage. I'm not certain though what to give the unaligned. Any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:23:27-07:00","id":900878,"title":"","content":"If I'm not mistaken, the advantages don't kick in until you start earning status among that covenant. For example, you need Status 2 before they'll trust you with their signature discipline, if they have one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:38:44-07:00","id":900895,"title":"","content":"You get to spend your xp on other stuff. I never saw having the ability to spend xp on something special as a bonus, more of a flavor choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:48:43-07:00","id":900906,"title":"","content":"Personnally, I don't get too involved in the mechanical advantages joining a covenant earns. The most interesting aspect if what it brings the character, how it influences the way they see things and who they can consider potential allies and enemies. I don't do the Invictus oaths and the carthian law because I thing there's no reason they should exist. Ideally, I'd argue covenant status dots could very well be granted rather than bought (status dots at creation are another thing since they give a real advantage from the start). The way the rules present all that is just a set of general pointers.<br /> <br /> So what would a non-aligned vampire get ? Depends on the setting. A city run by a particularly fanatical LeS government might chase them away or blood bind them if they refuse to join. In a city where all five covenants coexist with the Prince being an invictus (for example) careful to not piss off anyone too much, a non-aligned might be pretty sought after. They're an outsider to all that political group mess, their interests lie elsewhere. If they prove they can handle themselves they could be seen as a potential ally by any of those covenants, especially if they don't particularly look for political power.<br /> <br /> An unaligned vampire is minding his own business when someone comes to him &quot;Hey, you there, we know you don't really like us Invictus guys, but we've sure you've noticed how that Acolyte is looking for trouble and messing with us lately and we know you had a few problems with him before. You could help us... neutralize him, hell, you can get part of his territory if you do a good job&quot;. Of course, the territory in question is not very big or populated, but it's better than nothing (and the character might stumble upon something the invictus missed that makes it much more valuable than it was thought) and it stands between Circle and Invictus territories which might put the unaligned in the middle of further political strife.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think it's more interesting to rule that it's not because you're not part of a covenant that you can't be friends with them. Sure, they won't share their mystical secrets, but they might temporarily support you if they have something to gain, and some of them might become real allies which might create some drama if they're ordered to act against you later.<br /> <br /> <br /> To answer more simply, not belonging to a covenant will not get you any of the matching advantages, but the GM can find a way to get you something anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T07:07:45-07:00","id":900919,"title":"","content":"You have an immediate benefit at character creation: not having to waste merit dots on a set of Status merits. You can put those into other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T07:37:56-07:00","id":900949,"title":"","content":"Also, a lack of a humanity breaking point. That's also nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T07:45:40-07:00","id":900958,"title":"","content":"What's the benefit in real life for not getting a job and the benefits that entails? Having more free time.. that's all. Choosing to go unaligned doesn't have to give you mechanical advantaged specifically for it, which is not &quot;you don't get these disadvantages brought upon by joining a covenant&quot;. Like duties expectations and whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:43:18-07:00","id":901020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/900875-what-you-should-get-for-not-joining-a-covenant?p=900949#post900949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a lack of a humanity breaking point. That's also nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>where is that in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:45:34-07:00","id":901022,"title":"","content":"When you join a covenant, you suffer a breaking point. By not joining, you avoid that breaking point. I don't remember where it is offhand","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:46:56-07:00","id":901023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/900875-what-you-should-get-for-not-joining-a-covenant#post900875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems not right that not joining a covenant would not give any game mechanic advantage. I'm not certain though what to give the unaligned. Any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You looking for 1E feedback or 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T10:09:40-07:00","id":901110,"title":"","content":"Pg 107 2E<br /> Humanity 5 (Three Dice)<br /> Two weeks active without human contact.<br /> Reaching Blood Potency 3.<br /> Death of a mortal family member.<br /> Joining a covenant to the point of gaining Status for it.<br /> <br /> I agree with the others. Not having to spend dots at creation ( or later ) to buy status dots to buy the discipline dots. Not having to hit that breaking point, is also nice. I think that while it closes some doors ( to secrets and such ) it does open doors too. You are not tied up in all that political posturing and that you have more you time to do what you want rather than having to listen to someone else. As S. Brechen said, People in covenants might help you here and there if they have something to gain.<br /> <br /> I think being in a covenant is not a one up on people who arent. So they dont need to have that mechanical discipline or status dots. You just spend your exp in different ways. It's more up to the story to handle the differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T10:29:25-07:00","id":901136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/900875-what-you-should-get-for-not-joining-a-covenant?p=900895#post900895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get to spend your xp on other stuff. I never saw having the ability to spend xp on something special as a bonus, more of a flavor choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the big thing, there's nothing mechanical that the covenants give that doesn't cost XP. This includes Allies/Contacts/whatever, except for the occasional piece of equipment or information that, let's be honest, the Storyteller was going to give you anyway.<br /> <br /> Now, are there benefits to joining a covenant beside the XP-expenditure ones? Yes, but nothing that is actually unavailable to the Unaligned, except maybe for a seat on the Primogen council to go by 1e. Heck, if an Unaligned vampire is old enough and politically powerful enough they might be in a good position to become Prince in a multiple-covenant city, it just takes more work than doing so with the backing of a covenant.<br /> <br /> I'll agree that some of the covenant benefits are really snazzy, I love the Coils of the Dragon and Theban Sorcery (not so big on Cruac), and find Invinctus Oaths rather neat (as the only benefit where the XP expenditure can be from someone else). Carthian Law was a letdown for me, but I like it in theory, and do like at least one of the merits.<br /> <br /> Now, in 1e the Invinctus and the Carthians got reduced Merit costs for certain merits, which is a much more variable advantage (it can be really good or really bad), and so it might be worthwhile either changing that or giving the unaligned some bonus if playing 1e (I like the idea of cheaper Contacts dots to represent knowing people everywhere). In 2e there's really no need to give them a bonus, as you can increase your Obfuscate or pick up some contacts when those covenant boys are buying their Cruac or their Night Doctor Surgery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T10:44:29-07:00","id":901147,"title":"","content":"Well, there are some XP breaks. Kind of. The Ordo Dracul have a merit that lets you get free Herd with every dot of Status/Mystery Cult. So, I mean, it costs you some XP, but you get lots back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:26:32-07:00","id":901194,"title":"","content":"This is a thing in almost every CofD line. It sucks to be Unaligned, a Ghost Wolf, Orderless or part of a Nameless Order, etc. Vampire is actually one of the cases where it's least harsh to opt out of a Y-Splat. Sure you don't qualify for as many purchases, but at least you don't miss out on any freebies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:39:09-07:00","id":901208,"title":"","content":"Is it really so bad that non aligned vampires don't get the little game mechanics plus the covenants have ? I mean, it's not like we're talking about a tournament fighter where all the characters have to be as balanced as possible. We're not talking about a character being unplayable if they don't join a political/religious group. Not to mention belonging to a covenant isn't a bonus if you're in a city where that covenant doesn't exist or is actiely chased. An aspiring Lancea et Sanctum in a Carthian/Circle ruled city might not even find someone to teach them any ritual.<br /> <br /> This is actually appropriate. You don't want to join anyone, well, you're not expected to help advance any of their agendas (and you're unlikely to be targetted as part of a political struggle), but you won't be privy to the little secrets unless you earn someone's trust with actual actions and favors and you'll only be able to count on yourself and your closest allies when you're in trouble. Freedom has its price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T18:03:53-07:00","id":901590,"title":"","content":"Maybe the benefit of unaligned is you eventually become a badass elder, like Zagreus or the Unholy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T04:19:57-07:00","id":901942,"title":"","content":"I was always partial to the Blind Queen myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T08:06:00-07:00","id":907104,"title":"","content":"Im A ok with being Unbound being a net disad, this leaves room for elders to spit on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T13:46:21-07:00","id":907269,"title":"","content":"What do you get for not having a job, or not joining a fraternity, or not having citizenship?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T17:24:24-07:00","id":907336,"title":"","content":"OK: <i>why</i> is joining a Convenant a Humanity Breaking Point? Answer that, and you <i>just might</i> have an answer to the OP's query. Or not; I wouldn't know without the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T11:27:59-07:00","id":907754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/900875-what-you-should-get-for-not-joining-a-covenant?p=907336#post907336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK: <i>why</i> is joining a Convenant a Humanity Breaking Point? Answer that, and you <i>just might</i> have an answer to the OP's query. Or not; I wouldn't know without the details.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The covenants are <i>inhuman</i>, and demand that their members think more like immortal monsters than like living human beings. The Circle of the Crone are the most obviously monstrous covenant, since they explicitly revel in being inhuman predators, and the Ordo Dracul, likewise, embraces a philosophy that exalts the vampiric condition and more or less explicitly rejects the notion of trying to cling to or recapture one's humanity. The Lancea et Sanctum are sort of the other side of that coin, sincerely believing that they are already damned for their sins, and that their existence as vampires is more or less a version of hell.<br /> <br /> The Invictus and the Carthian movement are built on less obviously inhuman philosophies, especially since the latter explicitly draws inspiration from modern mortal political theories. However, both &quot;political&quot; Covenants are fundamentally concerned with their vision of what's best for the Kindred, with little regard for the needs or desires of the mortals around them, whom they generally regard more as tools and expendable pawns than as individuals worthy of respect.<br /> <br /> In short, all of the Covenants demand that their members turn their backs on their mortal lives and identities, or at least encourage them to do so. A neonate might join a covenant solely for companionship or to gain a measure of protection from the other power-players in the city, but even if the young vampire doesn't entirely buy his covenant's &quot;party line&quot; he's still human enough that he'll have a basic desire to fit in with his chosen group and to earn the esteem of his peers.<br /> <br /> To paraphrase Nietzsche, he who hangs out with monsters should look to it that he himself does not become a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T07:19:27-07:00","id":909145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/900875-what-you-should-get-for-not-joining-a-covenant?p=907336#post907336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK: <i>why</i> is joining a Convenant a Humanity Breaking Point? Answer that, and you <i>just might</i> have an answer to the OP's query. Or not; I wouldn't know without the details.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to acknowledge you're no longer human to apply for a membership with a No Mortals Allowed organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T09:32:43-07:00","id":909224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/900875-what-you-should-get-for-not-joining-a-covenant?p=907269#post907269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you get for not having a job, or not joining a fraternity, or not having citizenship?</div> </div> </div> </div>More free time for the first two, and being free from the expectation or illusion (as applicable to the true nature of the governing body) someone else will protect your rights for the third. Very similar to the Unbound, actually.<br /> <br /> Thank you, I love answering rhetorical questions.<br /> <br /> To say what the Unbound inherently get is this:<ul><li>The time to focus on maintaining Humanity and pretend to be human/perfect their Masquerade</li> <li>Attempts by covenants to recruit them, with the attention and love-bombing gifts used to get the Unbound to join their cult</li> <li>Freedom from Humanity breaking points caused by joining a covenant, and the other breaking points from associating with psychotic vampires of the covenants</li> </ul>I don't think you should give mechanical benefits for non-membership in Covenants unless you want to make a broad statement about the nature of the covenants that is backed up real in-game realities. Remember, game mechanics are the physics of the plots and stories and by redefining them you redefine the fundamental nature of the game world.<br /> <br /> If I were to make a statement about the difference between being in a covenant and not, it'd be belonging to a covenant means letting go of denial about your transformation, and denial is a powerful tool to resist change, in this case change into a monster. Humanity or Touchstone would be the mechanics I would choose to affect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-07-2016, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}